# Temporal Testing - Complete Implementation Guide

**

## Testing Philosophy

Testing Temporal applications requires a different approach than traditional applications because of the distributed, durable nature of workflows. This guide covers comprehensive testing strategies for all Temporal components.

## Testing Pyramid for Temporal

```
         ┌─────────────────────┐
         │   E2E Tests         │  ← Few tests, full integration
         │   (Production-like) │
         └─────────────────────┘
              ┌───────────────────────┐
              │  Integration Tests    │  ← Workflow + Activities
              │  (Test Environment)   │
              └───────────────────────┘
                   ┌────────────────────────┐
                   │   Unit Tests           │  ← Many tests, fast
                   │   (Activities, Logic)  │
                   └────────────────────────┘
```

## Unit Testing Activities

### TypeScript Activity Tests

```typescript
// activities.ts
export async function sendEmail(to: string, subject: string): Promise<void> {
  const transporter = nodemailer.createTransport({
    host: process.env.SMTP_HOST,
  });
  
  await transporter.sendMail({
    from: 'test@example.com',
    to,
    subject,
  });
}

// activities.test.ts
import { sendEmail } from './activities';
import nodemailer from 'nodemailer';

jest.mock('nodemailer');

describe('sendEmail activity', () => {
  let mockSendMail: jest.Mock;

  beforeEach(() => {
    mockSendMail = jest.fn().mockResolvedValue({});
    (nodemailer.createTransport as jest.Mock).mockReturnValue({
      sendMail: mockSendMail,
    });
  });

  it('sends email with correct parameters', async () => {
    await sendEmail('user@example.com', 'Test Subject');
    
    expect(mockSendMail).toHaveBeenCalledWith({
      from: 'test@example.com',
      to: 'user@example.com',
      subject: 'Test Subject',
    });
  });

  it('throws error when email service fails', async () => {
    mockSendMail.mockRejectedValue(new Error('SMTP error'));
    
    await expect(
      sendEmail('user@example.com', 'Test')
    ).rejects.toThrow('SMTP error');
  });
});
```

